Don't worry.

550
00:49:09,366 --> 00:49:12,099
We will make them pay for all of that!

551
00:49:12,933 --> 00:49:14,632
Will you?

552
00:49:30,433 --> 00:49:34,665
Or are you going to leave
that to Yakup Bey, too?

553
00:49:45,833 --> 00:49:47,999
Welcome to our palace, Lord's daughter.

554
00:49:48,000 --> 00:49:49,799
Yeah right.

555
00:49:52,433 --> 00:49:55,799
I will never forget that you
brought me here like a slave!

556
00:50:01,333 --> 00:50:04,432
I know your memory is strong.

557
00:50:04,700 --> 00:50:06,599
You never forget.

558
00:50:07,900 --> 00:50:09,065
Come on.

559
00:50:16,066 --> 00:50:17,799
Cerkutay.

560
00:50:21,300 --> 00:50:22,699
I waited!

561
00:50:24,733 --> 00:50:28,199
I waited for my Bey and my brothers to come!

562
00:50:28,200 --> 00:50:29,432
You didn't!

563
00:50:30,400 --> 00:50:31,732
None of you did!

564
00:50:36,633 --> 00:50:38,299
Cerkutay...

565
00:50:39,433 --> 00:50:41,365
We looked for you.

566
00:50:42,466 --> 00:50:43,899
Don't say that.

567
00:50:44,066 --> 00:50:46,065
I'd never leave you!

568
00:50:47,633 --> 00:50:49,132
We looked everywhere.

569
00:50:49,266 --> 00:50:52,165
If Osman Bey looked for me.

570
00:50:53,433 --> 00:50:57,032
He'd find me even if
I was buried under ground.

571
00:50:58,666 --> 00:51:01,732
You left me at the hands
of the infidels, my Bey!

572
00:51:11,200 --> 00:51:12,299
Cerkutay...

573
00:51:13,866 --> 00:51:15,099
My valiant...

574
00:51:17,166 --> 00:51:18,365
Cerkutay...

575
00:51:19,333 --> 00:51:20,645
Look at me!

576
00:51:21,200 --> 00:51:22,192
Look at me.

577
00:51:22,733 --> 00:51:24,032
Look at me.

578
00:51:24,366 --> 00:51:26,065
I know you the best.

579
00:51:27,166 --> 00:51:29,032
I understand you.

580
00:51:31,533 --> 00:51:32,932
You don't know anything.

581
00:51:36,400 --> 00:51:37,599
I was a valiant.

582
00:51:38,200 --> 00:51:39,932
I was an Alp!

583
00:51:41,633 --> 00:51:43,565
I fought until...

584
00:51:43,566 --> 00:51:46,165
...the last drop of my blood.

585
00:51:50,633 --> 00:51:51,865
I fell captive.

586
00:51:54,466 --> 00:51:56,965
I lived with rats and dogs!

587
00:51:56,966 --> 00:51:59,365
They tortured my whole body.

588
00:51:59,666 --> 00:52:00,765
I didn't give up.

589
00:52:04,600 --> 00:52:06,932
I never backed down on my duty.

590
00:52:06,933 --> 00:52:08,899
I didn’t speak one word.

591
00:52:10,433 --> 00:52:11,299
Cerkutay.

592
00:52:11,533 --> 00:52:14,299
I completed my duty Osman Bey.

593
00:52:14,900 --> 00:52:17,399
I did what a good Alp would!

594
00:52:22,366 --> 00:52:24,465
Did you do what a Bey would, Osman Bey?

595
00:52:25,966 --> 00:52:28,165
What did you do Osman Bey?

596
00:52:30,733 --> 00:52:33,632
Everyone's talking about us out there.

597
00:52:33,633 --> 00:52:36,232
They're disrespecting us.

598
00:52:39,866 --> 00:52:40,865
Cerkutay.

599
00:52:43,366 --> 00:52:46,232
Do you know
why they're disrespecting us?

600
00:52:48,800 --> 00:52:49,999
For whom?

601
00:52:50,700 --> 00:52:51,899
For whom, my valiant?

602
00:52:53,400 --> 00:52:56,399
Do you know why we were trapped?

603
00:52:56,633 --> 00:52:58,549
I don't know about you.

604
00:52:58,800 --> 00:52:59,999
But I..

605
00:53:00,533 --> 00:53:02,732
...fell for your cause.

606
00:53:13,466 --> 00:53:14,699
Cerkutay.

607
00:53:15,666 --> 00:53:17,965
Come on! Go now.

608
00:53:18,400 --> 00:53:20,799
Go and get some rest.
Go.

609
00:53:21,800 --> 00:53:23,699
It's too painful to hear it, eh?

610
00:53:27,500 --> 00:53:28,465
I lived that.

611
00:53:29,900 --> 00:53:32,765
You can't even stand to hear it.

612
00:53:47,166 --> 00:53:48,032
Come on Cerkutay.

613
00:53:50,000 --> 00:53:51,132
Leave.

614
00:53:53,366 --> 00:53:54,965
Leave Cerkutay.

615
00:53:55,800 --> 00:53:56,765
Leave.

616
00:54:07,666 --> 00:54:09,132
I'm sorry, my Bey

617
00:54:09,600 --> 00:54:10,699
He is not...

618
00:54:14,933 --> 00:54:15,932
Osman Bey...

619
00:54:16,633 --> 00:54:18,632
He'll calm down in time.

620
00:54:24,433 --> 00:54:25,432
My Bey!

621
00:54:32,133 --> 00:54:32,932
Boran.

622
00:54:33,166 --> 00:54:35,665
Go with him.
Don't leave him alone.

623
00:54:36,166 --> 00:54:37,665
Sure my Bey.

624
00:54:40,233 --> 00:54:41,965
I am joyless, can't eat.

625
00:54:51,666 --> 00:54:52,565
My Bey

626
00:55:10,000 --> 00:55:11,232
Holofira?

627
00:55:33,166 --> 00:55:36,032
A place with a huge garden!

628
00:55:37,799 --> 00:55:39,365
What a shame!

629
00:55:46,000 --> 00:55:49,465
You couldn't fit in that huge palace!

630
00:55:49,733 --> 00:55:53,632
But you fit my whole family
in this room huh!?

631
00:56:33,500 --> 00:56:35,599
All that time.

632
00:56:36,799 --> 00:56:39,132
Nights bled into days...

633
00:56:40,100 --> 00:56:43,165
...days bled into nights.

634
00:56:52,066 --> 00:56:53,499
Don't do this.

635
00:56:53,500 --> 00:56:55,732
Don't do what Ulgen?

636
00:56:59,000 --> 00:57:00,599
Don't do what?

637
00:57:02,633 --> 00:57:03,632
What about you?

638
00:57:05,600 --> 00:57:09,532
I left you in our home
Why did you come here?

639
00:57:11,416 --> 00:57:12,416
I...

640
00:57:13,100 --> 00:57:17,732
Osman Bey didn't want us to stay there
all by ourselves while you're gone.

641
00:57:17,966 --> 00:57:21,265
We came here to stay until you come back.

642
00:57:27,000 --> 00:57:28,298
I'm back.

643
00:57:32,000 --> 00:57:35,155
I'm back. I'm back.

644
00:57:39,133 --> 00:57:40,965
Go gather your stuff

645
00:57:40,966 --> 00:57:42,665
We're leaving.

646
00:57:57,866 --> 00:57:59,365
Sister Ulgen

647
00:58:01,100 --> 00:58:03,298
You take my niece and leave

648
00:58:03,299 --> 00:58:06,599
Let me fulfill my longing with my brother.

649
00:58:22,833 --> 00:58:24,665
Osman Bey is very mad about this.

650
00:58:24,666 --> 00:58:27,132
Your son looted my caravan
with bunch of looters!

651
00:58:27,133 --> 00:58:30,199
They tried to sell me off like a slave!

652
00:58:32,799 --> 00:58:36,899
Orhan Bey must have an excuse
for what you've gone through.

653
00:58:37,500 --> 00:58:39,665
Don't worry Holofira.

654
00:58:39,666 --> 00:58:42,032
We will cover your losses.

655
00:58:42,033 --> 00:58:45,099
I dont want gold from you, Malhun Hatun.

656
00:58:46,799 --> 00:58:49,332
I want to go back home.

657
00:58:51,233 --> 00:58:52,865
I understand you Holofira.

658
00:58:52,866 --> 00:58:55,165
But don’t raise your voice.

659
00:58:56,500 --> 00:58:59,065
Don't forget who you're talking to.

660
00:59:07,299 --> 00:59:10,732
You can go back home
whenever you want

661
00:59:11,933 --> 00:59:14,032
Isn't that right Orhan Bey?

662
00:59:14,400 --> 00:59:15,599
Holofira

663
00:59:19,533 --> 00:59:21,432
You can't go now

664
00:59:22,700 --> 00:59:24,665
-Firstly...
-Firstly...

665
00:59:29,333 --> 00:59:31,432
...you need to rest Holofira.

666
00:59:31,700 --> 00:59:33,532
You look very tired.

667
00:59:33,833 --> 00:59:36,399
They will accompany you to your room

668
00:59:36,400 --> 00:59:37,999
Am I a hostage...

669
00:59:38,000 --> 00:59:41,265
or a guest who can leave
whenever she wants?

670
00:59:44,600 --> 00:59:46,565
You're our guest girl

671
00:59:47,033 --> 00:59:48,965
We dont keep our hostages
in our palace...

672
00:59:48,966 --> 00:59:51,499
...but in our dungeon.

673
01:00:04,966 --> 01:00:08,298
How can you make my mother talk
with that disrespectful girl, brother?

674
01:00:08,299 --> 01:00:09,699
Fatma!

675
01:00:11,500 --> 01:00:13,798
Watch the words...

676
01:00:14,700 --> 01:00:16,065
coming out of your mouth.

677
01:00:16,066 --> 01:00:17,432
Orhan!

678
01:00:17,433 --> 01:00:18,798
Mother!

679
01:00:18,900 --> 01:00:19,765
Don't...

680
01:00:20,166 --> 01:00:23,032
...don't even think about
sending Holafira.

681
01:00:23,833 --> 01:00:25,532
Are you still talking about her?

682
01:00:25,900 --> 01:00:28,732
What are you going to do with
a woman who doesn't even want you?

683
01:00:28,833 --> 01:00:30,565
She has clearly moved on!

684
01:00:30,733 --> 01:00:33,132
Stop it!

685
01:00:35,366 --> 01:00:37,465
Tell me, Orhan Bey...

686
01:00:38,600 --> 01:00:41,232
...did you complete youi mission?

687
01:00:42,900 --> 01:00:45,999
May I come in Malhun Haton?

688
01:00:46,966 --> 01:00:48,665
Come in!

689
01:00:52,600 --> 01:00:55,665
Osman Bey wants to see Orhan Bey.

690
01:01:17,400 --> 01:01:19,199
The brother I had...

691
01:01:19,666 --> 01:01:22,832
...wouldn't have left me behind!

692
01:01:23,466 --> 01:01:26,732
How could you leave me behind Boran Bey?

693
01:01:27,799 --> 01:01:29,665
Don't say that brother!

694
01:01:29,866 --> 01:01:32,699
We searched everywhere we could for you!

695
01:01:32,896 --> 01:01:33,896
I...

696
01:01:36,233 --> 01:01:39,399
I Cerkutay...

697
01:01:40,066 --> 01:01:45,332
I endured tortures
for all these years by myself!

698
01:01:46,000 --> 01:01:47,699
I was given no food!

699
01:01:47,866 --> 01:01:50,865
or water!

700
01:01:51,133 --> 01:01:53,399
I even lost my arm!

701
01:01:58,333 --> 01:02:02,565
But I didn't sell you out!

702
01:02:05,200 --> 01:02:07,432
I didn't speak a single word!
A single word!

703
01:02:07,833 --> 01:02:09,798
Not even a single word!

704
01:02:11,566 --> 01:02:13,932
Neither about Osman Bey..

705
01:02:14,133 --> 01:02:17,965
nor about the people
I thought were my brothers!

706
01:02:18,966 --> 01:02:21,189
I didn’t sell you out.

707
01:02:22,166 --> 01:02:24,225
Brother

708
01:02:27,666 --> 01:02:30,332
It wasn't the enemy that broke me...

709
01:02:32,733 --> 01:02:35,899
...it was the fact that
I had no one, Boran!

710
01:02:45,133 --> 01:02:47,732
Don't say anything else now.

711
01:03:12,900 --> 01:03:16,632
What did you do about the flagless, Orhan?

712
01:03:17,866 --> 01:03:20,365
Earning their trust...

713
01:03:23,133 --> 01:03:25,742
...seemed difficult my Bey.

714
01:03:26,900 --> 01:03:30,399
Did you expect it to be easy, Orhan?

715
01:03:33,233 --> 01:03:37,965
I attacked a Caravan with them..

716
01:03:40,433 --> 01:03:44,932
...to show them my skills
and earn their favor.

717
01:03:49,433 --> 01:03:52,132
I'm asking you if the job is done or not.

718
01:03:52,666 --> 01:03:55,199
I'm not asking you about anything else

719
01:03:57,433 --> 01:03:59,232
It's not done yet, my Bey.

720
01:03:59,433 --> 01:04:01,365
...but it will be.

721
01:04:03,266 --> 01:04:05,765
Why are you here then, Orhan?

722
01:04:06,233 --> 01:04:09,232
How are you going to persuade the Flagless?

723
01:04:11,000 --> 01:04:14,199
I will show them that
as long as they're flagless(without country)...

724
01:04:15,100 --> 01:04:18,665
no treasure will give
them comfort, my Bey.

725
01:04:19,066 --> 01:04:20,865
That's going to be my move.

726
01:04:22,433 --> 01:04:24,932
I would have done it by now, but...

727
01:04:27,033 --> 01:04:28,199
...Something I didn't expect-

728
01:04:28,200 --> 01:04:32,042
The Hatun you didn't expect to be there
is now here in the palace.

729
01:04:41,100 --> 01:04:44,999
The Caravan I attacked with the Flagless...

730
01:04:45,633 --> 01:04:49,065
..turned out to be Holafira's caravan,
my Bey.

731
01:04:51,433 --> 01:04:56,365
I couldn't leave her there father.

732
01:05:08,266 --> 01:05:11,665
So you became hope
for someone who needed it.

733
01:05:21,200 --> 01:05:23,732
But even though you did that...

734
01:05:25,500 --> 01:05:29,432
...that still doesn't mean
you can just fail your mission.

735
01:05:46,066 --> 01:05:48,632
Wait for me in the yard tomorrow morning.

736
01:05:49,633 --> 01:05:51,298
As you command my Bey.

737
01:06:04,666 --> 01:06:07,365
Caravansarai

738
01:06:07,833 --> 01:06:10,665
They must be asleep now. Come on Huseyin.

739
01:06:11,733 --> 01:06:13,899
Don't forget what I told you.

740
01:06:13,900 --> 01:06:15,665
As you command Gonca Hatun.

741
01:06:32,933 --> 01:06:34,965
What's this map for, my Sultan?

742
01:06:36,600 --> 01:06:39,432
The map of Seljuk treasure.

743
01:07:45,666 --> 01:07:48,565
You...
Who are you?

744
01:07:58,433 --> 01:08:01,032
-Alps!
-Catch him!

745
01:08:04,233 --> 01:08:07,132
Alps!
Wake up!

746
01:08:27,233 --> 01:08:28,765
Who are you?

747
01:08:50,200 --> 01:08:53,999
Close all the exits!
No one will leave!

748
01:08:58,000 --> 01:08:58,865
My shahzade(Prince)!

749
01:08:58,866 --> 01:09:00,299
Baysungur!

750
01:09:00,500 --> 01:09:02,999
Search all the rooms, come on!

751
01:09:03,500 --> 01:09:05,064
Alps! Come on!

752
01:09:05,265 --> 01:09:09,599
Until we find where that dog hides
we will knock every door!

753
01:09:26,765 --> 01:09:28,999
Watch it Alaeddin Bey!

754
01:09:29,100 --> 01:09:31,499
This is Gonca Hatun's room!

755
01:09:32,399 --> 01:09:33,064
She is sleeping!

756
01:09:33,066 --> 01:09:35,398
Then call her and wake her up!

757
01:09:35,399 --> 01:09:38,799
No one will sleep until I find
the dog that entered my room!

758
01:09:39,399 --> 01:09:42,599
Alaeddin Bey why are you shouting
in front of my door!?

759
01:09:42,800 --> 01:09:44,965
I want to search your room Gonca Hatun.

760
01:09:45,800 --> 01:09:47,965
A bandit entered my room.

761
01:09:48,933 --> 01:09:51,099
Were your alps out for a night stroll?

762
01:09:54,133 --> 01:09:57,432
Whatever...
Come inside, there is no one in there.

763
01:10:13,400 --> 01:10:17,432
Tell your alps to be
more careful Alaeddin Bey.

764
01:10:18,866 --> 01:10:22,132
Well they don t teach you that
in the Madrasah, right?

765
01:10:34,866 --> 01:10:36,065
Alps...

766
01:10:36,700 --> 01:10:39,499
I don't want this to happen again.

767
01:10:40,066 --> 01:10:41,599
As you command my shahzade(Prince).

768
01:10:41,900 --> 01:10:43,632
Get back to your duties now.

769
01:10:45,366 --> 01:10:46,199
Come on.

770
01:10:51,400 --> 01:10:54,499
You are not as smart as me,
madrasah student!

771
01:11:07,466 --> 01:11:09,032
Alaeddin!

772
01:11:10,100 --> 01:11:11,599
Alaeddin!

773
01:11:25,700 --> 01:11:28,765
You can't outsmart me, Hatun.

774
01:11:37,733 --> 01:11:39,465
She says I am not a prisoner!

775
01:11:41,433 --> 01:11:43,499
I'd be in a dungeon if I were a prisoner!

776
01:11:45,300 --> 01:11:46,665
What's the difference?

777
01:12:00,300 --> 01:12:01,432
Orhan.

778
01:12:02,200 --> 01:12:04,399
This is all your fault.

779
01:12:26,833 --> 01:12:28,132
Holofira.

780
01:12:31,233 --> 01:12:32,932
You changed a lot.

781
01:12:35,500 --> 01:12:37,032
But still...

782
01:12:37,500 --> 01:12:39,965
...your eyes still look the same.

783
01:12:40,400 --> 01:12:43,099
This Hatun is mine now.

784
01:12:49,233 --> 01:12:50,865
No one touches her...

785
01:12:51,400 --> 01:12:53,632
before going past me.

786
01:12:57,966 --> 01:12:59,699
Don't be stupid Holofira!

787
01:13:00,666 --> 01:13:02,899
Don't be stupid Holofira!
Get it together!

788
01:13:03,466 --> 01:13:04,665
Pull yourself together!

789
01:13:10,000 --> 01:13:11,865
You didn't forget him...

790
01:13:18,466 --> 01:13:20,199
...but he never looked for you.

791
01:13:21,300 --> 01:13:22,465
He never came.

792
01:13:25,400 --> 01:13:27,432
He's not the Orhan you're waiting for.

793
01:13:29,866 --> 01:13:32,932
He's just a forager who raided your caravan.

794
01:13:49,666 --> 01:13:51,065
Kismet!

795
01:13:53,400 --> 01:13:54,699
I'm here, my Hatun.

796
01:13:57,566 --> 01:13:58,699
Kismet.

797
01:14:02,700 --> 01:14:04,432
In the name of Allah,
the merciful, the compassionate.

798
01:14:11,566 --> 01:14:14,132
I haven't walked
outside in months.

799
01:14:15,700 --> 01:14:17,465
I'm sick of it.

800
01:14:20,133 --> 01:14:21,332
Let's go outside tomorrow.

801
01:14:22,533 --> 01:14:24,465
I need to get some air.

802
01:14:25,366 --> 01:14:26,599
But Bala Hatun...

803
01:14:26,600 --> 01:14:28,599
You heard what I said Kismet.

804
01:14:30,333 --> 01:14:31,632
Get ready.

805
01:14:33,833 --> 01:14:35,132
As you wish.

806
01:15:02,500 --> 01:15:04,965
I stopped but the enemy won't.

807
01:15:15,166 --> 01:15:17,232
I've been fighting for a long time.

808
01:15:17,600 --> 01:15:20,699
But I haven't seen a man who fights
as good as you my Bey.

809
01:15:23,700 --> 01:15:25,699
Praising the enemy is a weapon.

810
01:15:26,466 --> 01:15:28,699
The arrogance will cause mistakes.

811
01:15:36,666 --> 01:15:38,165
You learned that well

812
01:15:41,500 --> 01:15:43,199
But It doesn't work on me.

813
01:16:01,666 --> 01:16:03,832
Slander and insult

814
01:16:10,933 --> 01:16:12,699
It leads the enemy to doubt.

815
01:16:12,700 --> 01:16:14,932
And doubt makes you make mistakes.

816
01:16:23,133 --> 01:16:25,665
Just like the Flagless do.

817
01:16:35,666 --> 01:16:38,399
They wanted to make you do
a raid with slander.

818
01:16:38,400 --> 01:16:39,965
And the result?

819
01:16:41,300 --> 01:16:43,065
The result is defeat.

820
01:17:33,800 --> 01:17:35,499
It's hard times...

821
01:17:36,833 --> 01:17:38,932
I don't want any mistakes Orhan.

822
01:17:38,933 --> 01:17:40,932
As you wish my bey.

823
01:17:44,500 --> 01:17:46,232
Take this.

824
01:18:06,500 --> 01:18:07,999
Here my bey

825
01:18:08,633 --> 01:18:09,832
Thank you

826
01:18:09,833 --> 01:18:12,032
The name of Allah the merciful,
the compassionate.

827
01:18:25,366 --> 01:18:26,365
My Bey...

828
01:18:29,233 --> 01:18:30,999
Cerkutay...

829
01:18:34,766 --> 01:18:36,299
Yes'?

830
01:18:38,833 --> 01:18:40,565
I can't convince him my Bey.

831
01:18:40,900 --> 01:18:43,132
He insists on leaving.

832
01:18:57,066 --> 01:19:00,365
If he doesn't believe in us anymore...

833
01:19:01,866 --> 01:19:03,932
...then let him.

834
01:19:11,500 --> 01:19:13,765
May Allah wish his future be bright.

835
01:19:15,933 --> 01:19:17,399
-Boran!
-My bey

836
01:19:17,400 --> 01:19:18,799
Send word to the tribe.

837
01:19:18,800 --> 01:19:20,565
The alps will be inspected!

838
01:19:20,566 --> 01:19:21,932
Tomorrow will be tough!

839
01:19:21,933 --> 01:19:23,765
As you wish my bey.

840
01:19:44,900 --> 01:19:46,265
Cerkutay

841
01:19:49,700 --> 01:19:52,199
Should you rethink maybe?

842
01:19:53,600 --> 01:19:54,865
Where will we go?

843
01:19:54,866 --> 01:19:57,699
I said we will leave Ulgen!

844
01:19:59,200 --> 01:20:01,865
I can't stay another night at this palace!

845
01:20:02,366 --> 01:20:03,732
This is our home!

846
01:20:03,733 --> 01:20:07,232
Why are we leaving?
If you want it so much you leave

847
01:20:10,400 --> 01:20:12,032
Cerkutay!

848
01:20:12,333 --> 01:20:14,032
How can you say that to your father?

849
01:20:14,033 --> 01:20:16,065
He s making us leave our home mother!

850
01:20:16,066 --> 01:20:18,499
Why don't you get mad at him?

851
01:20:35,100 --> 01:20:36,899
Do you not want to leave?

852
01:20:36,900 --> 01:20:38,999
No! Everyone is here.

853
01:20:39,000 --> 01:20:40,299
Osman Bey.

854
01:20:40,300 --> 01:20:41,532
Uncle Boran!

855
01:20:41,533 --> 01:20:42,699
Uncle Gurbuz!

856
01:20:42,700 --> 01:20:44,932
Sister Fatma!
All of them are here.

857
01:20:45,133 --> 01:20:46,799
What am I going to do without them?

858
01:20:46,900 --> 01:20:48,799
What about me?

859
01:20:50,700 --> 01:20:52,299
Did you not miss me?

860
01:20:52,400 --> 01:20:54,499
I did miss you but...

861
01:20:55,133 --> 01:20:57,832
I don't even know you.

862
01:21:13,866 --> 01:21:16,399
This palace is not the place
for you to get to know me.

863
01:21:16,766 --> 01:21:18,599
What does that mean?

864
01:21:26,366 --> 01:21:30,175
Don't you want to become an Alp?

865
01:21:30,966 --> 01:21:32,255
I do!

866
01:21:33,800 --> 01:21:36,732
Let s go and get to know each other then.

867
01:21:38,333 --> 01:21:41,232
I will teach you how to become an Alp.

868
01:21:41,966 --> 01:21:44,765
No one can do it better than I do!

869
01:21:45,700 --> 01:21:47,699
Cerkutay Alp!

870
01:21:52,300 --> 01:21:53,999
Good then.

871
01:21:54,366 --> 01:21:57,065
Let's go Cerkutay Bey.

872
01:22:03,433 --> 01:22:06,065
GERMIYANIDS BORDER

873
01:22:13,533 --> 01:22:15,265
If Osman Bey still refuses to obey...

874
01:22:15,466 --> 01:22:19,299
...after Gonca is back from Konya, my Bey...

875
01:22:25,300 --> 01:22:27,599
May I come in my Bey'?

876
01:22:27,833 --> 01:22:30,132
Come in, son!

877
01:22:32,033 --> 01:22:34,182
Are we all set?

878
01:22:35,100 --> 01:22:37,165
We are, my Bey.

879
01:22:37,433 --> 01:22:40,832
Ten thousand horsemen
are waiting at Cukuragzi.

880
01:22:41,000 --> 01:22:43,665
They are waiting but...

881
01:22:44,366 --> 01:22:47,465
...are we really going to attack Yenisehir?

882
01:22:47,833 --> 01:22:50,465
The last thing I want...

883
01:22:51,566 --> 01:22:54,232
...is to spill the blood of my own.

884
01:23:00,166 --> 01:23:02,632
However....

885
01:23:03,533 --> 01:23:06,699
Osman made the first move against us.

886
01:23:08,900 --> 01:23:13,199
The meal he invited us to
might as well be an ambush.

887
01:23:13,600 --> 01:23:15,832
Stay here then.

888
01:23:16,066 --> 01:23:18,632
I will go destroy Osman.

889
01:23:19,466 --> 01:23:20,965
Mehmet!

890
01:23:21,933 --> 01:23:23,595
Son!

891
01:23:24,600 --> 01:23:26,632
While all the Beys are going to be there

892
01:23:27,000 --> 01:23:32,199
I have to show up especially after
I made my intention to be the Sultan.

893
01:23:36,366 --> 01:23:39,499
Don't worry.

894
01:23:42,166 --> 01:23:45,899
We're prepared for anything.

895
01:23:50,300 --> 01:23:52,332
My Mehmet...

896
01:23:52,533 --> 01:23:56,932
Thousands of Alps with you as their commander.

897
01:23:57,966 --> 01:24:01,565
That's all the security we need son.

898
01:24:02,133 --> 01:24:04,532
We're going to go there.

899
01:24:05,100 --> 01:24:10,299
Sit around their table and
look them in their eyes.

900
01:24:12,933 --> 01:24:16,499
If Osman makes a move on our lives...

901
01:24:18,666 --> 01:24:22,832
Then you will then attack Yenisehir.

902
01:24:24,900 --> 01:24:28,999
You will leave no human being alive!

903
01:24:29,900 --> 01:24:32,899
I ignored about the arrow shot at you my Bey.

904
01:24:33,233 --> 01:24:37,565
...but if they make
the slightest attempt on your life...

905
01:24:38,600 --> 01:24:42,165
...no one can stop what will happen next.

906
01:25:09,200 --> 01:25:10,759
Let's go.

907
01:25:16,200 --> 01:25:20,105
So you're saying that those who set me and Orhan up
now trapped Alaeddin in Konya...

908
01:25:20,105 --> 01:25:21,032
Right.

909
01:25:21,333 --> 01:25:24,065
I can't wait for him to be back.

910
01:25:27,000 --> 01:25:28,932
Don't worry.

911
01:25:29,466 --> 01:25:32,099
Don't worry at all.

912
01:25:33,800 --> 01:25:36,332
My son is clever.

913
01:25:36,900 --> 01:25:40,965
Alaeddin will be fine even if they attack him.

914
01:25:41,556 --> 01:25:43,332
Well...

915
01:25:43,800 --> 01:25:46,132
it's not the enemy w
e're competing against

916
01:25:46,266 --> 01:25:49,132
We're competing against our own.

917
01:25:49,666 --> 01:25:51,865
This is just the beginning.

918
01:25:57,600 --> 01:25:59,765
I want everything to be all set Malhun.

919
01:26:00,000 --> 01:26:02,232
Make sure we have everything
we need tonight.

920
01:26:03,700 --> 01:26:06,999
The sherbet and the food are ready, my Bey

921
01:26:07,400 --> 01:26:10,132
...but it looks like you
mean something else.

922
01:26:11,066 --> 01:26:12,899
Don't worry.

923
01:26:12,900 --> 01:26:15,499
We will take measurements
in the palace, too.

924
01:26:15,966 --> 01:26:19,632
When Konur brings Remus tonight...

925
01:26:20,733 --> 01:26:22,965
...things will come to a conclusion.

926
01:26:34,233 --> 01:26:37,099
You were just dried herbs.

927
01:26:37,500 --> 01:26:40,799
...and when cooked the remedy
hidden within you came out.

928
01:26:44,733 --> 01:26:47,365
If you ask whose remedy this is...

929
01:26:52,633 --> 01:26:55,432
....the answer is the one
that looks for a remedy.

930
01:27:03,900 --> 01:27:05,032
Bala Hatun.

931
01:27:06,700 --> 01:27:09,965
Come have a seat at my table.

932
01:27:10,700 --> 01:27:13,632
We can't refuse an invitation Dervish Efendi.

933
01:27:13,966 --> 01:27:15,232
Thank you.

934
01:27:15,600 --> 01:27:17,199
But how do you know my name?

935
01:27:17,733 --> 01:27:21,239
It would be a shame if I didn't know
the name of the Sheikh Edebali's daughter.

936
01:27:21,239 --> 01:27:22,299
Have a seat

937
01:27:27,333 --> 01:27:28,699
You have a seat as well.

938
01:27:41,766 --> 01:27:44,299
You brought some herbs to the lodge.

939
01:27:45,400 --> 01:27:46,732
Thank you.

940
01:27:54,633 --> 01:27:59,332
But I'm used to living with
this illness Dervish.

941
01:28:01,766 --> 01:28:03,265
In the name of Allah,
the merciful, the compassionate.

942
01:28:06,933 --> 01:28:09,432
Getting used to is different...

943
01:28:10,300 --> 01:28:12,699
...than being patient.

944
01:28:12,933 --> 01:28:14,765
Like Hadrat Eyyub...

945
01:28:14,766 --> 01:28:16,699
Bala Hatun.

946
01:28:18,933 --> 01:28:21,099
Eyyub Hadrath

947
01:28:21,100 --> 01:28:25,632
had many blessings for 80 years.

948
01:28:26,433 --> 01:28:29,032
He had many kids

949
01:28:29,800 --> 01:28:31,032
many possessions

950
01:28:31,700 --> 01:28:33,332
but

951
01:28:33,333 --> 01:28:35,932
a test for him came along.

952
01:28:36,533 --> 01:28:38,232
One night..

953
01:28:38,233 --> 01:28:41,032
while his family was sleeping...

954
01:28:41,233 --> 01:28:44,099
Eyyub's home was demolished.

955
01:28:44,733 --> 01:28:46,799
Ten of his kids...

956
01:28:46,800 --> 01:28:49,299
...were under the wreck.

957
01:28:49,800 --> 01:28:51,765
He suffered a lot.

958
01:28:53,300 --> 01:28:55,699
But his test was not over.

959
01:28:56,400 --> 01:28:58,732
One day he woke up and..

960
01:28:59,133 --> 01:29:02,132
saw that he had boils all over him.

961
01:29:03,233 --> 01:29:06,265
No doctor could find a cure.

962
01:29:06,866 --> 01:29:08,832
Days went by...

963
01:29:09,100 --> 01:29:14,032
...and Eyub Hadrath's body
was covered in scars

964
01:29:15,733 --> 01:29:19,965
But he was like a mulberry leaf, Eyub Hadrath.

965
01:29:21,433 --> 01:29:26,865
The same way the mulberry leaf remains calm
as it transforms into cloth.

966
01:29:27,733 --> 01:29:30,265
...he too remained calm
and didn't complain.

967
01:29:31,100 --> 01:29:33,999
It s said that eighteen years went by...

968
01:29:34,800 --> 01:29:37,132
All the doctors were desperate...

969
01:29:37,433 --> 01:29:40,065
...as none of the ointments worked.

970
01:29:40,433 --> 01:29:44,432
His body was covered in nothing but scars.

971
01:29:45,533 --> 01:29:50,899
His wife Rahime came to him one day
and said that "Oh Eyub...

972
01:29:52,533 --> 01:29:57,599
...just pray so that Allah
saves you from your troubles"

973
01:29:59,633 --> 01:30:03,099
Eyub looked at his wife and said that.

974
01:30:03,100 --> 01:30:06,532
"How can I ask for such a thing?"

975
01:30:07,400 --> 01:30:12,799
"He gave me 80 years filled with joy
of my children and prosperity"

976
01:30:13,966 --> 01:30:17,332
"How can I complain now?"

977
01:30:18,166 --> 01:30:21,232
"Let me suffer for another 80 years"

978
01:30:22,066 --> 01:30:26,099
...and then I might consider that"

979
01:30:29,866 --> 01:30:31,899
Eyyub Hadrath.

980
01:30:32,433 --> 01:30:36,265
...was a prophet.
He had companions.

981
01:30:36,666 --> 01:30:40,232
And this trouble benefited the devil.

982
01:30:40,800 --> 01:30:44,265
He poisoned the hearts of his companions.

983
01:30:44,933 --> 01:30:46,899
They started talking.

984
01:30:47,300 --> 01:30:51,199
"What kind of prophet
can't find a remedy for himself?"

985
01:30:51,766 --> 01:30:53,999
"Where is the miracle?"

986
01:30:55,700 --> 01:30:58,532
They abandoned Eyyub one by one.

987
01:31:00,300 --> 01:31:04,799
But Eyyub Hadrath did not complain.

988
01:31:05,600 --> 01:31:09,732
Years passed his wounds
were festered with maggots

989
01:31:11,400 --> 01:31:14,665
The maggots reached his hearts and tongue

990
01:31:16,466 --> 01:31:21,132
Then Eyyub's heart was filled with fear.

991
01:31:23,266 --> 01:31:26,365
"If the maggots eat my heart and tongue..

992
01:31:27,233 --> 01:31:29,032
how can I pray?"

993
01:31:30,733 --> 01:31:32,732
He prayed to Allah

994
01:31:33,733 --> 01:31:37,665
and great Allah rewarded his patience.

995
01:31:38,633 --> 01:31:41,499
...by healing his wounds.

996
01:31:42,333 --> 01:31:45,899
He had more children than the ones he lost.

997
01:31:46,500 --> 01:31:49,932
He was rewarded with more richness.

998
01:31:58,800 --> 01:32:01,599
Like Hadrath Eyyub...

999
01:32:02,100 --> 01:32:04,399
...those who wait patiently.

1000
01:32:05,933 --> 01:32:08,232
...good news come soon Bala Hatun.

1001
01:32:08,800 --> 01:32:10,999
I pray that...

1002
01:32:12,566 --> 01:32:15,099
...you will find your remedy
with these herbs.

1003
01:32:22,200 --> 01:32:24,899
Thank you dervish.

1004
01:32:26,500 --> 01:32:29,032
It's already giving me strength.

1005
01:33:01,833 --> 01:33:04,632
6 great Beys will sit on each table

1006
01:33:05,433 --> 01:33:08,099
The heart of the Turkmens will beat here!

1007
01:33:08,833 --> 01:33:13,032
They will all feel as if they are in
their own homeland, but..

1008
01:33:15,133 --> 01:33:17,332
...they will see that...

1009
01:33:17,933 --> 01:33:22,132
...the one who will unite these lands
is Osman Bey.

1010
01:33:25,366 --> 01:33:27,565
You will put the famous furs of Esrefoglus there.

1011
01:33:27,666 --> 01:33:28,765
Yes my Bey

1012
01:33:28,900 --> 01:33:30,899
You will put carpets of the Karesioglus there.

1013
01:33:30,900 --> 01:33:32,099
Yes my Bey.

1014
01:33:32,333 --> 01:33:33,865
Come here brother.

1015
01:33:36,666 --> 01:33:39,899
You know what you are going to do for
Germiyanid Yakup Bey.

1016
01:33:40,100 --> 01:33:41,399
We know my Bey.

1017
01:33:41,900 --> 01:33:43,232
Come on

1018
01:33:44,400 --> 01:33:46,232
Beys are about to arrive.

1019
01:33:47,833 --> 01:33:49,232
Brothers

1020
01:33:50,933 --> 01:33:55,899
if anything goes wrong,
you will all pay for that

1021
01:33:56,233 --> 01:33:58,232
As you command Boran Bey!

1022
01:33:58,666 --> 01:34:00,199
Come on.

1023
01:34:08,800 --> 01:34:11,199
Come on sisters!

1024
01:34:20,700 --> 01:34:22,999
You have guests?

1025
01:34:27,833 --> 01:34:30,832
Go to your room I will prepare
something to wear for you.

1026
01:34:31,433 --> 01:34:34,032
There is no need Fatma Hatun.

1027
01:34:36,100 --> 01:34:37,999
Who are the guests?

1028
01:34:38,000 --> 01:34:40,332
The Turkmen Beys in the border lands.

1029
01:34:43,333 --> 01:34:45,799
I will send your meal to your room

1030
01:34:47,400 --> 01:34:50,899
You don't want your guests to see me?

1031
01:34:59,400 --> 01:35:00,599
Well...

1032
01:35:01,166 --> 01:35:03,399
...how are you going
to introduce me right?

1033
01:35:04,166 --> 01:35:07,799
The loot your bandit brother got from the pillage?

1034
01:35:09,166 --> 01:35:12,465
Don't call my brother a bandit again!

1035
01:35:13,066 --> 01:35:15,265
-Or...
-Or?

1036
01:35:15,800 --> 01:35:17,665
What are you going to do?

1037
01:35:18,500 --> 01:35:20,399
Fatma!

1038
01:35:34,300 --> 01:35:35,765
Excuse her.

1039
01:35:37,666 --> 01:35:39,065
I'm not mad at her.

1040
01:35:39,800 --> 01:35:40,832
I'm mad at you.

1041
01:35:42,200 --> 01:35:44,565
When can I go home, Orhan?

1042
01:35:56,966 --> 01:35:58,999
I'll take you myself.

1043
01:35:59,766 --> 01:36:00,999
But have patience.

1044
01:36:05,700 --> 01:36:07,732
These are hard times.

1045
01:36:15,033 --> 01:36:16,232
How’s your wound?

1046
01:36:19,033 --> 01:36:20,332
Which one are you asking?

1047
01:36:25,300 --> 01:36:26,832
Either!

1048
01:37:06,533 --> 01:37:07,632
She's crazy

1049
01:37:39,033 --> 01:37:40,199
O Allah!

1050
01:37:54,066 --> 01:37:56,099
You can't go anywhere...

1051
01:37:56,100 --> 01:37:58,065
...before you speak.

1052
01:37:59,500 --> 01:38:01,599
Yavuz! You traitor!

1053
01:38:04,433 --> 01:38:05,232
Aykurt!

1054
01:38:07,666 --> 01:38:09,032
Tie this dog's hands.

1055
01:38:13,233 --> 01:38:14,932
As long as he lives...

1056
01:38:14,933 --> 01:38:16,932
...they won't stop.

1057
01:38:17,566 --> 01:38:20,165
He won't die until
we get what we want from Remus.

1058
01:38:20,400 --> 01:38:22,165
Come on!
We're going to Yenisehir.

1059
01:39:39,933 --> 01:39:41,265
Peace be with you.

1060
01:39:42,200 --> 01:39:43,632
Peace be upon you too.

1061
01:39:45,833 --> 01:39:46,899
Welcome.

1062
01:39:48,333 --> 01:39:49,599
We're glad you're here.

1063
01:39:49,600 --> 01:39:52,265
Thank you Osman Bey!

1064
01:40:01,066 --> 01:40:03,132
Thank you Osman bey

1065
01:40:04,666 --> 01:40:06,599
You prepared well.

1066
01:40:07,066 --> 01:40:09,199
You greeted us with kindness.

1067
01:40:09,566 --> 01:40:11,699
There are so many Beys here.

1068
01:40:13,933 --> 01:40:16,465
We did what's necessary Yakup Bey.

1069
01:40:19,300 --> 01:40:20,732
-Turahan
-My Bey?

1070
01:40:22,266 --> 01:40:23,232
Go on.

1071
01:40:23,466 --> 01:40:25,232
Come Yakup Bey.

1072
01:40:40,733 --> 01:40:41,932
Orhan.

1073
01:40:42,266 --> 01:40:43,365
My Bey.

1074
01:40:43,366 --> 01:40:45,432
You will wait for Remus

1075
01:40:45,433 --> 01:40:46,965
This will end tonight.

1076
01:40:46,966 --> 01:40:49,032
It will be a tough night, huh?

1077
01:40:49,033 --> 01:40:51,132
As you wish my bey.

1078
01:40:53,600 --> 01:40:55,432
Osman Bey

1079
01:41:37,700 --> 01:41:40,799
Here, here hatuns.

1080
01:41:43,300 --> 01:41:45,465
Welcome hatuns.

1081
01:41:45,766 --> 01:41:48,099
MashAllah, mashAllah.

1082
01:41:48,100 --> 01:41:51,699
You built a palace worthy of
your name Malhun Hatun

1083
01:41:51,700 --> 01:41:54,865
Until dinner please have a seat here.

1084
01:42:14,700 --> 01:42:17,399
Welcome Saadet Hatun.

1085
01:42:26,566 --> 01:42:28,199
Have a seat there.

1086
01:42:53,700 --> 01:42:56,565
Good work Malhun Hatun.

1087
01:42:57,066 --> 01:42:59,132
The palace turned out nice.

1088
01:43:00,666 --> 01:43:02,832
Thank you.

1089
01:43:11,000 --> 01:43:12,799
Hatuns..

1090
01:43:16,300 --> 01:43:17,699
Fitnat!

1091
01:43:18,866 --> 01:43:23,499
Prepare 100 rolls of our fabrics
for Malhun Hatun.

1092
01:43:24,300 --> 01:43:27,265
Once these walls are decorated
with those...

1093
01:43:27,266 --> 01:43:28,965
...then...

1094
01:43:28,966 --> 01:43:31,932
...it will really look like a palace.

1095
01:43:32,933 --> 01:43:35,732
Thank you Saadet Hatun.

1096
01:43:36,233 --> 01:43:39,999
But we don't need anything
more than this.

1097
01:43:40,733 --> 01:43:45,465
All the fabrics are have have been woven
by our great Kayi hatuns

1098
01:43:48,766 --> 01:43:51,865
You can give those fabrics to our hatuns.

1099
01:44:03,633 --> 01:44:05,465
Here Yakup Bey.

1100
01:44:12,466 --> 01:44:13,965
Here, Karesi Bey.

1101
01:44:13,966 --> 01:44:15,132
Candar Bey.

1102
01:44:15,133 --> 01:44:16,399
Here.

1103
01:44:20,633 --> 01:44:22,499
Felekuddin Bey, here please.

1104
01:44:23,166 --> 01:44:25,399
Mubanzeddin Bey here please.

1105
01:44:33,333 --> 01:44:36,199
Is this a new tradition Osman Bey?

1106
01:44:36,200 --> 01:44:39,832
Even our places have been decided beforehand.

1107
01:44:41,966 --> 01:44:43,899
It's quite good

1108
01:44:44,666 --> 01:44:46,532
From now on...

1109
01:44:47,200 --> 01:44:50,232
...everything has an order.

1110
01:44:50,766 --> 01:44:55,365
You made it look like our patterns, praise be!

1111
01:44:55,366 --> 01:44:57,465
You must know of it Osman Bey.

1112
01:44:57,466 --> 01:44:59,465
These lands...

1113
01:44:59,466 --> 01:45:02,099
were visited by many of our blood.

1114
01:45:02,400 --> 01:45:04,099
Some of them...

1115
01:45:05,333 --> 01:45:08,565
...didn't take our land as their own.

1116
01:45:09,533 --> 01:45:12,032
They thought of us as strangers.

1117
01:45:12,566 --> 01:45:14,599
The moves they made..

1118
01:45:15,533 --> 01:45:18,132
...disturbed our order.

1119
01:45:23,200 --> 01:45:24,232
So...

1120
01:45:24,633 --> 01:45:26,132
...that's why...

1121
01:45:26,133 --> 01:45:28,432
...we didn't want
you to feel strange.

1122
01:45:29,733 --> 01:45:32,232
Recognize our home...

1123
01:45:33,266 --> 01:45:34,965
...as your own...

1124
01:45:36,266 --> 01:45:38,065
...Recognize us as...

1125
01:45:38,066 --> 01:45:41,799
...one of your own, if Allah permits.

1126
01:45:50,800 --> 01:45:52,165
Yakup Bey.

1127
01:45:53,533 --> 01:45:57,632
Why is there no Germiyanid
mark on your spot'?

1128
01:46:03,333 --> 01:46:04,799
Allah Allah!

1129
01:46:04,933 --> 01:46:06,565
-Boran!
-My Bey!

1130
01:46:06,866 --> 01:46:09,465
How could you miss such a detail?

1131
01:46:09,700 --> 01:46:12,332
Forgive me, my Bey.

1132
01:46:14,866 --> 01:46:15,765
It's okay.

1133
01:46:16,766 --> 01:46:19,865
Such small mistakes can take place.

1134
01:46:23,466 --> 01:46:25,765
Kanyumaz!

1135
01:46:43,300 --> 01:46:45,899
Well, then.

1136
01:46:46,033 --> 01:46:48,599
Let's take our seats.

1137
01:46:56,300 --> 01:46:59,065
Don't worry my Beys.

1138
01:47:00,733 --> 01:47:04,565
Every piece of land I sit on
is Germiyanid land.

1139
01:47:08,966 --> 01:47:11,399
Your home...

1140
01:47:11,600 --> 01:47:13,199
..is my home.

1141
01:47:14,133 --> 01:47:16,499
Thank you.

1142
01:47:17,600 --> 01:47:20,832
That's what we wanted to tell you.

1143
01:47:24,900 --> 01:47:29,365
From now on all of our moves...

1144
01:47:31,233 --> 01:47:33,299
...will be based on that fact, if Allah permits.

1145
01:47:36,066 --> 01:47:37,799
- Boran!
- My Bey.

1146
01:47:38,100 --> 01:47:40,199
Bring the sherbet here.

1147
01:47:40,400 --> 01:47:42,032
As you command, my Bey

1148
01:47:42,333 --> 01:47:44,032
Go on.

1149
01:47:55,900 --> 01:47:57,532
I have news from Mehmet Bey.

1150
01:47:57,666 --> 01:48:00,932
The Alps have surrounded Yenisehir, my Bey

1151
01:48:12,466 --> 01:48:13,932
Here my Bey.

1152
01:48:14,433 --> 01:48:16,432
Thank you, thank you.

1153
01:48:17,433 --> 01:48:19,132
Enjoy it.

1154
01:48:22,933 --> 01:48:25,965
In the name of Allah
the merciful, the compassionate.

1155
01:48:38,966 --> 01:48:43,565
We heard that you're going to be staying
at the borders for some time Saadet Hatun.

1156
01:48:44,200 --> 01:48:46,199
What you heard is right.

1157
01:48:46,800 --> 01:48:49,265
There's much work to do
around the borders.

1158
01:48:49,533 --> 01:48:52,232
We will be around for some time.

1159
01:48:53,866 --> 01:48:57,665
We'll see each other more often then,
Saadet Hatun

1160
01:49:00,533 --> 01:49:02,765
Indeed.

1161
01:49:11,133 --> 01:49:13,532
Who is the pretty girl, Malhun Hatun?

1162
01:49:14,000 --> 01:49:16,565
Is she your daughter in law?

1163
01:49:22,599 --> 01:49:23,865
Daughter in law?

1164
01:49:23,966 --> 01:49:26,199
We didn't know.

1165
01:49:26,599 --> 01:49:28,999
Is she Orhan Bey's wife?

1166
01:49:33,566 --> 01:49:36,632
Holafira is our guest here.

1167
01:49:39,666 --> 01:49:42,265
Princess Holafira.

1168
01:49:47,700 --> 01:49:50,732
As Malhun Hatun said

1169
01:49:51,900 --> 01:49:53,699
I'm a guest here.

1170
01:49:53,966 --> 01:49:58,199
I thought that Malhun Hatun
had Orhan marry a foreigner'

1171
01:50:02,033 --> 01:50:04,125
You've got some funny jokes, don't you?

1172
01:50:17,200 --> 01:50:22,132
What brought you to these lands
princess Holofira?

1173
01:50:28,900 --> 01:50:30,232
Trade.

1174
01:50:33,400 --> 01:50:37,232
I came here to trade like you.

1175
01:50:54,466 --> 01:50:55,665
Get up.

1176
01:51:07,300 --> 01:51:08,999
How are the preparations?

1177
01:51:09,366 --> 01:51:11,132
The weapons are on the way, sir.

1178
01:51:11,599 --> 01:51:15,199
Our traders that earned their trust
hide the weapons among other goods.

1179
01:51:16,900 --> 01:51:20,032
We tolerated them for a reason all these years.

1180
01:51:34,566 --> 01:51:37,832
These bottles will explode
in the places they think the safest.

1181
01:51:54,099 --> 01:51:56,965
These swords will cut the people
they love the most.

1182
01:52:05,300 --> 01:52:07,199
Soldiers of Jesus Christ!

1183
01:52:07,633 --> 01:52:10,799
There wont be any soldier left
that does not hold a sword!

1184
01:52:11,366 --> 01:52:13,332
Your neighbors...

1185
01:52:14,300 --> 01:52:18,199
...your alp friends
the people you dined with...

1186
01:52:19,500 --> 01:52:22,365
...those who tried to assimilate us for years!

1187
01:52:22,500 --> 01:52:24,799
They will die by our hands!

1188
01:52:25,633 --> 01:52:27,899
They won't sleep anymore!

1189
01:52:28,800 --> 01:52:30,732
Because we are awake!

1190
01:52:38,166 --> 01:52:39,598
Tell me Tesehus.

1191
01:52:40,200 --> 01:52:41,532
What about the other locations'?

1192
01:52:41,733 --> 01:52:44,932
50 more joined us in Karacahisar.

1193
01:52:45,433 --> 01:52:49,532
And the Christians in Sogut
are ready to fight beside us.

1194
01:52:50,066 --> 01:52:54,432
Master Vasilis,
the fire of rebellion you lit...

1195
01:52:55,000 --> 01:52:57,098
...is growing each day.

1196
01:52:57,800 --> 01:52:59,699
It will grow...

1197
01:53:00,633 --> 01:53:02,532
It will giow bigger...

1198
01:53:03,833 --> 01:53:06,865
Everything will be ready before grand master arrives.

1199
01:53:09,099 --> 01:53:10,699
Are you ready to destroy the Turks!?

1200
01:53:10,700 --> 01:53:12,199
We are!

1201
01:53:13,933 --> 01:53:15,565
Jesus Christ is with us!

1202
01:53:18,633 --> 01:53:20,265
Gonca Hatun.

1203
01:53:22,166 --> 01:53:24,165
Is one of your alps is missing?

1204
01:53:24,500 --> 01:53:27,032
Your memory is strong, student.

1205
01:53:27,666 --> 01:53:31,865
Yes I don't forget what I read,
and what I see.

1206
01:53:32,599 --> 01:53:35,132
I sent a messenger to my Bey father.

1207
01:53:38,133 --> 01:53:40,098
Why are you so curious?

1208
01:53:40,700 --> 01:53:43,665
Do you think the bandit that entered
your room was one of us?

1209
01:53:44,633 --> 01:53:47,432
Why would you send an alp in my room?

1210
01:53:48,300 --> 01:53:50,032
There is nothing you can take from me.

1211
01:53:50,433 --> 01:53:51,732
Right?

1212
01:53:54,800 --> 01:53:59,465
If I had sent an alp
I would have taken what I wanted, student.

1213
01:54:00,833 --> 01:54:03,565
It looks like there was a plan.

1214
01:54:05,266 --> 01:54:07,832
There is someone close to me
that likes playing games...

1215
01:54:08,166 --> 01:54:11,699
Forget about games now!
Show me your skills.

1216
01:54:12,233 --> 01:54:14,665
Let's see if your mind is strong enoug
h to control your horse, too!

1217
01:54:14,666 --> 01:54:15,865
Come on!

1218
01:54:17,666 --> 01:54:20,465
You don't know me at all, Gonca Hatun.

1219
01:54:20,700 --> 01:54:22,299
Come on!

1220
01:54:23,066 --> 01:54:24,499
He is just like his father.

1221
01:54:27,866 --> 01:54:29,965
We will follow them from a distance.

1222
01:54:30,200 --> 01:54:32,098
We will, tool Come on!

1223
01:54:32,300 --> 01:54:33,899
Come on!

1224
01:54:43,300 --> 01:54:46,232
May peace and mercy of Allah be upon you.

1225
01:54:48,300 --> 01:54:51,799
May peace and mercy of Allah be upon you

1226
01:55:13,466 --> 01:55:14,632
Mother!

1227
01:55:21,233 --> 01:55:22,399
Alaeddin Ali?

1228
01:55:30,366 --> 01:55:31,365
Son

1229
01:55:32,333 --> 01:55:33,598
Mother

1230
01:55:33,599 --> 01:55:34,499
Son

1231
01:55:36,700 --> 01:55:39,499
Don't son You'll get sick Alaeddin

1232
01:55:45,233 --> 01:55:47,332
I can't take it mother.

1233
01:55:48,566 --> 01:55:50,432
I miss you so much.

1234
01:55:50,700 --> 01:55:52,165
I miss you!

1235
01:55:53,333 --> 01:55:53,999
Mother.

1236
01:55:55,233 --> 01:55:56,365
Mother!

1237
01:56:09,700 --> 01:56:11,132
Are you okay?

1238
01:56:12,500 --> 01:56:15,065
You're okay! Praise be!

1239
01:56:15,533 --> 01:56:17,032
If you're okay!

1240
01:56:17,300 --> 01:56:18,532
I'm okay.

1241
01:56:19,033 --> 01:56:20,532
You'll be okay, right mother?

1242
01:56:25,533 --> 01:56:26,299
Mother?

1243
01:56:27,033 --> 01:56:28,432
Sit down.

1244
01:56:32,633 --> 01:56:34,032
Drink it mother.

1245
01:56:34,566 --> 01:56:36,399
Mother.

1246
01:56:37,733 --> 01:56:38,999
Drink it.

1247
01:56:42,633 --> 01:56:44,199
Tell me son.

1248
01:56:45,666 --> 01:56:47,565
How are things in Konya?

1249
01:56:47,666 --> 01:56:49,365
Konya's the same mother.

1250
01:56:50,966 --> 01:56:52,132
But Yakup Bey

1251
01:56:53,866 --> 01:56:55,432
...will cause trouble.

1252
01:56:57,133 --> 01:56:58,832
He sent his daughter to Konya.

1253
01:57:00,633 --> 01:57:01,899
I know son.

1254
01:57:02,866 --> 01:57:03,765
I know.

1255
01:57:05,200 --> 01:57:07,065
He causes trouble here too.

1256
01:57:07,166 --> 01:57:08,565
What is it mother'?

1257
01:57:10,400 --> 01:57:11,465
Yakup Bey

1258
01:57:14,133 --> 01:57:16,299
...asked your father to obey.

1259
01:57:23,666 --> 01:57:24,699
My Shehzade(Prince).

1260
01:57:25,866 --> 01:57:27,265
Get the horses ready

1261
01:57:28,200 --> 01:57:30,432
This silence is no good.

1262
01:57:32,733 --> 01:57:35,299
Until Yakup Bey leaves Yenisehir...

1263
01:57:35,400 --> 01:57:37,032
..we'll stay cautious.

1264
01:57:37,033 --> 01:57:38,465
As you wish my Shehzade(Prince).

1265
01:57:42,200 --> 01:57:44,665
Where are your sons Osman Bey?

1266
01:57:45,433 --> 01:57:46,799
I can't see them

1267
01:57:47,300 --> 01:57:48,999
They have a duty.

1268
01:57:49,566 --> 01:57:51,265
Your sons are absent as well.

1269
01:57:51,966 --> 01:57:53,032
What happened?

1270
01:57:53,300 --> 01:57:55,965
They are out to get me good news,
if Allah permits.

1271
01:57:56,333 --> 01:57:59,365
If Allah permits, if Allah permits.

1272
01:58:02,400 --> 01:58:04,032
Well...

1273
01:58:05,300 --> 01:58:06,965
Let's get to the case.

1274
01:58:10,400 --> 01:58:12,765
What's the sultan issue you have?

1275
01:58:14,066 --> 01:58:15,598
It's not an issue.

1276
01:58:16,466 --> 01:58:18,598
It's the truth Osman Bey.

1277
01:58:20,733 --> 01:58:21,899
What is it?

1278
01:58:22,099 --> 01:58:23,899
Do you have something to say?

1279
01:58:24,233 --> 01:58:25,899
Of course.

1280
01:58:28,166 --> 01:58:30,199
The hereditary rights...

1281
01:58:31,099 --> 01:58:34,532
...belonged to Sultan Mesut before he died.

1282
01:58:37,266 --> 01:58:38,598
It's clear...

1283
01:58:39,666 --> 01:58:41,699
And the Beys know that.

1284
01:58:43,633 --> 01:58:44,865
...you...

1285
01:58:46,200 --> 01:58:48,999
...haven't even paid Konya taxes for years.

1286
01:58:52,066 --> 01:58:53,699
Well...

1287
01:58:53,700 --> 01:58:57,232
Do you want to be the heir to Seljuk State...

1288
01:59:00,133 --> 01:59:01,732
...that you were never loyal to?

1289
01:59:02,366 --> 01:59:04,632
Victory comes from courage...

1290
01:59:05,500 --> 01:59:07,899
...not loyalty Osman Bey.

1291
01:59:11,000 --> 01:59:12,465
Maybe...

1292
01:59:12,466 --> 01:59:14,465
...Sultan Mesut and I...

1293
01:59:15,200 --> 01:59:16,699
...didn't get along...

1294
01:59:17,933 --> 01:59:19,098
...but..

1295
01:59:19,900 --> 01:59:22,632
...I walked a very straight path.

1296
01:59:25,400 --> 01:59:27,532
Beys know that as well.

1297
01:59:31,500 --> 01:59:33,365
You're right Yakup Bey.

1298
01:59:35,099 --> 01:59:36,165
You're right.

1299
01:59:37,233 --> 01:59:38,232
And...

1300
01:59:39,366 --> 01:59:41,098
...you lead the way to us too.

1301
01:59:42,800 --> 01:59:44,265
You say...

1302
01:59:45,033 --> 01:59:46,965
...that if you want to lead...

1303
01:59:48,000 --> 01:59:49,865
...you'll have to fight the leader!

1304
01:59:51,366 --> 01:59:52,999
You speak of courage!

1305
01:59:54,733 --> 01:59:56,299
Not loyalty.

1306
01:59:57,099 --> 01:59:58,432
Osman Bey.

1307
02:00:00,433 --> 02:00:02,365
I earned my freedom...

1308
02:00:02,800 --> 02:00:04,632
...with my own grace.

1309
02:00:07,433 --> 02:00:08,365
And you...

1310
02:00:09,333 --> 02:00:12,632
...took it from Sultan Mesut's hands.

1311
02:00:15,599 --> 02:00:16,499
Also...

1312
02:00:18,733 --> 02:00:21,465
Don't forget this:

1313
02:00:22,300 --> 02:00:23,965
Neither...

1314
02:00:23,966 --> 02:00:27,132
...am I Konya
who has surrendered to Mongols

1315
02:00:28,166 --> 02:00:30,665
...nor you are me.

1316
02:00:33,533 --> 02:00:36,499
Don't think I'm advising you something.

1317
02:00:38,366 --> 02:00:40,765
Every Bey here...

1318
02:00:40,766 --> 02:00:42,765
..in this invitation...

1319
02:00:43,166 --> 02:00:47,499
...have no choice but to follow my lead...

1320
02:00:54,333 --> 02:00:57,199
What if the path you're walking is wrong?

1321
02:00:57,200 --> 02:01:01,365
I saved you from
imprisonment, Osman Bey.

1322
02:01:03,233 --> 02:01:07,899
It's clear who's on the right path.

1323
02:01:09,033 --> 02:01:11,532
I'm not saying with bad intent.

1324
02:01:12,833 --> 02:01:14,865
During my rule as the Sultan...

1325
02:01:14,866 --> 02:01:17,399
...I don't wish for situations like this.

1326
02:01:17,400 --> 02:01:19,699
We're not afraid of shahada...

1327
02:01:19,700 --> 02:01:21,699
...we are not afraid of
imprisonment either!

1328
02:01:25,566 --> 02:01:27,565
Can I come in my bey?

1329
02:01:27,933 --> 02:01:29,765
Come in Boran

1330
02:01:38,700 --> 02:01:39,699
My bey

1331
02:01:39,700 --> 02:01:41,499
We have Remus.

1332
02:01:49,166 --> 02:01:51,399
With your permission beys.

1333
02:01:55,300 --> 02:01:57,799
You have the permission Osman Bey.

1334
02:02:00,300 --> 02:02:03,098
Go and come back swiftly.

1335
02:02:04,566 --> 02:02:07,165
We still have things to talk about.

1336
02:02:39,099 --> 02:02:43,299
Has it been decided when
the border market will open Saadet Hatun?

1337
02:02:43,533 --> 02:02:46,299
It will open in two days Hatice Hatun.

1338
02:02:48,866 --> 02:02:51,132
Haven't your caravans made it yet?

1339
02:02:51,133 --> 02:02:52,465
Sevilay Hatun?

1340
02:02:52,466 --> 02:02:55,299
They will be at the
border market tomorrow morning.

1341
02:02:59,866 --> 02:03:01,865
Can anyone...

1342
02:03:02,866 --> 02:03:04,865
...enter this border market?

1343
02:03:09,922 --> 02:03:11,352
Of course.

1344
02:03:13,099 --> 02:03:16,999
We will make agreements with the Lords
near the borders.

1345
02:03:17,000 --> 02:03:21,199
Caravans from India and
Constantinople will come.

1346
02:03:25,466 --> 02:03:27,765
Princess Holofira.

1347
02:03:28,133 --> 02:03:30,432
You said you were interested in trade.

1348
02:03:30,700 --> 02:03:32,799
We invite you too.

1349
02:03:35,833 --> 02:03:38,565
Holofira is here for a short time

1350
02:03:46,733 --> 02:03:49,899
We have high hopes
for the border market, Hatuns.

1351
02:03:49,900 --> 02:03:52,332
The better the goods...

1352
02:03:52,333 --> 02:03:55,098
...the greater our name will be.

1353
02:03:58,733 --> 02:04:01,899
Your stall is ready too, Malhun Hatun

1354
02:04:01,900 --> 02:04:04,199
Thank you Saadet Hatun.

1355
02:04:04,966 --> 02:04:09,098
You must've heard about
Yenisehir's name for trading.

1356
02:04:11,099 --> 02:04:12,499
I haven't.

1357
02:04:15,266 --> 02:04:18,765
Then your name hasn't made it
to Germiyan lands.

1358
02:04:28,033 --> 02:04:29,499
Speaking of which...

1359
02:04:29,633 --> 02:04:32,832
...what can Kayi do apart from rugs?

1360
02:04:35,433 --> 02:04:39,999
Then you'll see it yourself
at the market, Saadet Hatun.

1361
02:05:00,266 --> 02:05:01,865
Speak!

1362
02:05:05,500 --> 02:05:06,332
Tell me.

1363
02:05:11,166 --> 02:05:12,598
So you...

1364
02:05:12,866 --> 02:05:15,365
...were playing games behind my Bey huh?

1365
02:05:36,800 --> 02:05:38,999
Do you remember what I told you?

1366
02:05:39,700 --> 02:05:42,432
I told you that if you did
something behind my back.

1367
02:05:42,900 --> 02:05:45,499
I'd make you pay.

1368
02:05:45,833 --> 02:05:47,999
Do you remember?

1369
02:05:51,766 --> 02:05:54,465
It seems that you don't.

1370
02:05:56,033 --> 02:05:58,199
But you will now.

1371
02:06:13,966 --> 02:06:16,165
Come here!

1372
02:06:17,066 --> 02:06:19,265
Look at me!

1373
02:06:20,266 --> 02:06:22,265
Look at me!

1374
02:06:24,866 --> 02:06:26,065
Come here.

1375
02:06:31,046 --> 02:06:32,365
Give me that.

1376
02:06:36,599 --> 02:06:37,832
Look at me!

1377
02:06:38,033 --> 02:06:41,199
Didn't I tell you that I'd rip your tongue off?

1378
02:06:43,733 --> 02:06:46,699
Didn't I tell you that I'd carve your eyes out?

1379
02:06:48,599 --> 02:06:50,098
You're going to talk.

1380
02:06:50,333 --> 02:06:52,732
You are going to talk!

1381
02:06:57,900 --> 02:06:59,399
I can't

1382
02:07:00,933 --> 02:07:02,098
They'd kill me.

1383
02:07:02,500 --> 02:07:04,132
I'm the one that will kill you.

1384
02:07:04,233 --> 02:07:06,232
Not anyone else. Talk!

1385
02:07:07,900 --> 02:07:09,965
Yakup Beyl

1386
02:07:10,500 --> 02:07:13,732
Yakup Bey set it all up!

1387
02:07:19,400 --> 02:07:21,499
He did it to...

1388
02:07:21,700 --> 02:07:24,799
...destroy your reputation.

1389
02:07:28,200 --> 02:07:31,365
...If you're lying again...

1390
02:07:31,500 --> 02:07:34,765
The letter! It's in my pocket!

1391
02:07:36,300 --> 02:07:38,565
Check it out.

1392
02:07:48,900 --> 02:07:50,598
My Bey.

1393
02:07:51,366 --> 02:07:53,432
-Kanyumaz
-Stay still

1394
02:07:59,233 --> 02:08:03,299
Yakup's man Kanyumaz..

1395
02:08:04,466 --> 02:08:07,665
He gave me the letter.

1396
02:08:14,933 --> 02:08:17,065
Look at me

1397
02:08:18,033 --> 02:08:19,799
If this is a lie...

1398
02:08:20,000 --> 02:08:23,032
...It's the truth for Christ's sake!

1399
02:08:23,700 --> 02:08:27,332
Yakup Bey is behind it all

1400
02:08:50,233 --> 02:08:52,399
They're going to kill me.

1401
02:09:08,166 --> 02:09:10,732
Well Yakup Bey..

1402
02:09:31,599 --> 02:09:33,132
-Turan
-Konur Bey

1403
02:09:33,133 --> 02:09:35,665
Germiyanid Mehmet has surrounded Yenisehir.

1404
02:09:35,800 --> 02:09:38,365
Tell the Alps to be ready.

1405
02:09:39,400 --> 02:09:40,632
Turan.

1406
02:09:42,266 --> 02:09:45,732
Tell the Alps to prepare in secret.
Don't let the people find out

1407
02:09:46,033 --> 02:09:48,765
As you command Konur Bey.

1408
02:09:55,233 --> 02:09:58,065
Osman Bey is with Remus, Konur Bey.

1409
02:09:58,366 --> 02:10:00,299
Thank you Dark All.

1410
02:10:29,800 --> 02:10:31,632
My Bey!

1411
02:10:36,733 --> 02:10:38,332
My Beyl

1412
02:10:45,666 --> 02:10:47,199
My Beyl

1413
02:10:53,300 --> 02:10:58,899
Well you are going to give us
a big stall in this market right.

1414
02:10:59,400 --> 02:11:01,065
...my Sultan?

1415
02:11:01,233 --> 02:11:07,332
Not just you Karesi Bey.
All the Beys on this table...

1416
02:11:07,700 --> 02:11:10,499
...will have the biggest stalls.

1417
02:11:11,500 --> 02:11:15,765
But the size of your stalls..

1418
02:11:16,099 --> 02:11:18,432
...will be determined by..

1419
02:11:18,700 --> 02:11:21,432
...the number of alps
you bring to the conquests.

1420
02:11:58,700 --> 02:11:59,965
Osman Bey.

1421
02:12:01,833 --> 02:12:04,932
You invited all these Beys here.

1422
02:12:05,833 --> 02:12:08,098
And now you're holding a sword.

1423
02:12:08,866 --> 02:12:10,665
This is either intimidation.

1424
02:12:11,900 --> 02:12:14,232
Or it means there will be blood.

1425
02:12:15,000 --> 02:12:16,598
There will be.

1426
02:12:24,099 --> 02:12:26,299
A lot of blood will be shed.

1427
02:12:30,300 --> 02:12:33,265
Osman... Osman...

1428
02:12:34,200 --> 02:12:37,399
If you do something to my Bey.

1429
02:12:37,633 --> 02:12:40,565
I'll destroy
you with your city!

1430
02:12:44,300 --> 02:12:45,999
Yakup Bey

1431
02:12:47,866 --> 02:12:49,699
During your rule as the Sultan...

1432
02:12:49,700 --> 02:12:52,632
...you said that
there won't be an enslaved Bey.

1433
02:12:52,766 --> 02:12:53,799
...right?

1434
02:12:55,599 --> 02:12:58,232
Then tell the beys too.

1435
02:12:59,200 --> 02:13:01,632
Let them hear too.

1436
02:13:16,066 --> 02:13:18,598
Will your reign...

1437
02:13:20,833 --> 02:13:24,832
...include setting Beys up?

1438
02:13:31,700 --> 02:13:34,499
Will it include...

1439
02:13:35,766 --> 02:13:39,432
...attacking Beys due to your greed?

1440
02:13:49,033 --> 02:13:52,332
Will your sense of justice..

1441
02:13:56,099 --> 02:13:59,932
...become corrupted...

1442
02:14:02,933 --> 02:14:05,499
for power and might?

1443
02:14:08,133 --> 02:14:11,265
Your words will decide on...

1444
02:14:12,666 --> 02:14:15,465
...whose blood is about to be spilled.

1445
02:14:36,317 --> 02:14:42,997
Contact us for any inquiries: turkision@gmail.com